# sudosrv is built CGO-free, so the Go runtime links statically. That is a
# project-wide property, not a packaging shortcut: this module has no cgo
# dependencies at all, which is what keeps cross-compilation clean and lets the
# same binary run on any glibc or musl host. There is nothing to link
# dynamically against.
#
# The corresponding override for logsh is a stronger claim -- it is a login
# shell, so a dynamic linker that cannot resolve it locks every recorded
# account out of the host. See logsh.lintian-overrides.
sudosrv: statically-linked-binary [usr/bin/sudosrv]
